       <t indent="0" pn="section-3-1">The following syntax specification uses the augmented Backus-Naur
 Form (BNF) notation as specified in RFC 822.</t>
-      <t indent="0" pn="section-3-2">Except as noted otherwise, all alphabetic characters are case-
-insensitive.  The use of upper or lower case characters to define
+      <t indent="0" pn="section-3-2">Except as noted otherwise, all alphabetic characters are case-insensitive.  The use of upper or lower case characters to define
 token strings is for editorial clarity only.  Implementations <bcp14>MUST</bcp14>
 accept these strings in a case-insensitive fashion.</t>
